<section id="details" class="o-row c-prod__info c-prod__section u-white-bg">
    <section class="o-max o-max--1400">
        <div class="o-layout o-layout--large o-layout--reverse">

            <div class="o-layout__item u-1/2@tablet">

                <section class="c-prod__details">
                                            <section class="c-prod-boxout o-box c-prod__details c-prod__programme-wrap  u-has-bg-color u-sapphire-bg">
                            <div class="prod__programme">
                                <p class="c-small-label">Programme</p>
                                <p><strong>Verdi</strong> Don Carlo (1886 Modena version)</p>
                            </div>
                        </section>
                                                                <section class="c-prod-boxout o-box c-prod__details c-prod__performers-wrap  u-has-bg-color u-sapphire-bg" >
                            <div class="prod__performers">
                                <p class="c-small-label">Performers</p>
                                <p><strong>Gwyn Hughes Jones</strong> Don Carlo<br />
<strong>Elizabeth Llewellyn</strong> Elisabetta de Valois<br />
<strong>David Soar</strong> Filippo<br />
<strong>Patrick Alexander Keefe</strong> Rodrigo<br />
<strong>Anna Werle</strong> Eboli<br />
<strong>Narrator</strong> tbc<br />
<strong>The Fai Da Te Chorus &amp; </strong><strong>Orchestra </strong></p>
                            </div>
                        </section>
                                                                <section class="c-prod__details c-prod__links-wrap c-prod__links-wrap--desktop c-content-style">
                            <div class="prod__links">
                                <p class="c-small-label">Related Links</p>
                                <p><a href="http://www.faidateproductionsltd.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.faidateproductionsltd.com</a></p>
                            </div>
                        </section>
                                    </section>

            </div>

            <div class="o-layout__item u-1/2@tablet">

                <div class="c-content-style">
                                        <p>Enter the world of a 16th-century Spanish royal power struggle, unbridled passion, and religious fervour. Based on Schiller’s play of the same name, <strong>Verdi</strong>’s grand opera <strong><em>Don Carlo</em></strong> is a dark, epic masterpiece which centres around the tragic, forbidden love between Don Carlo and his stepmother, Elisabeth of Valois.</p>
<p>Featuring a dazzling line-up of international opera soloists and rising young stars, with a chorus including students from the<strong> Royal Conservatoire of Scotland</strong>, this evening presents the &#8216;best bits&#8217; of Verdi’s stirring opera, taking in themes of love, loyalty, familial dysfunction, destiny, brotherhood, and jealousy.</p>
<p>Leading the orchestra, comprised of players from the renowned <strong>Glyndebourne Sinfonia</strong>, is <strong>Matthew Kofi Waldren</strong>, a specialist in Italianate opera repertoire and fresh from his triumph conducting Puccini’s <em>La fanciulla del West</em> for London’s Opera Holland Park.</p>
<p><em>Fai Da Te Productions is a new production company which puts artists and storytelling at the heart of its work.</em></p>
                </div>

                                    <p class="c-prod__duration"><strong>Duration: </strong>2 hours 45 minutes (incl. interval)</p>
                
                
                                    <section class="c-prod__details c-prod__links-wrap c-prod__links-wrap--mobile c-content-style">
